Z||000000||Elenor84||12-11-2001||02:25 AM||||Hey guys...just curious if the 86 sway bar is better then the 84?  If so can they be swaped?<BR>Thx!<P>------------------<BR>Lance<BR>Click Image to go to site.<BR><A HREF="http://members.nbci.com/_XMCM/lancegspage/Index.html" TARGET=_blank> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Side1.jpg"> </A>||||reg||1
Z||000001||FieroJoe||12-11-2001||01:30 PM||||I believe it might depend on which suspension you have, either WS1 or WS6.  I know that the WS6 springs are tighter, but I do not know if they came with the 13/16" bar (compared to 5/8" stock??)  Either way, I <B>do</B> know that 88 suspensions have a larger bar up front, and the GT's and Formulas have a bar in back (smaller though, GM still wanted understeer), 88 coupes didnt come with rear bars.<P>I have a stock Fiero front bar in the rear, I think it was out of a 86.  It is the same size as my front.  Car still understeers, and its safe, but I can make the back end step out a lot easier. ||||reg||1
